Clicking an open window's taskbar button had no toggle behavior — it would only focus/restore, with no way to minimize via the taskbar.

## Changes

- **`src/App.tsx`**: Added `handleWindowClick` that implements toggle logic — minimizes if the clicked window is already active and visible, otherwise focuses/restores it. Passed to `Taskbar` in place of `focusWindow`.

```tsx
const handleWindowClick = (id: string) => {
  const win = windows.find((w) => w.id === id)
  if (win && win.id === activeWindowId && !win.isMinimized) {
    minimizeWindow(id)
  } else {
    focusWindow(id)
  }
}
```

## Pull Request Description

This PR resolves issue #28248 by introducing a modular, copy-paste ready React component: a FileUpload Dropzone with a Ripple Progress Indicator. It cleanly bridges native HTML5 Drag and Drop events into a React state machine, allowing EaseMotion CSS to orchestrate tactile physical feedback during drag operations, upload progress, and completion states.

Closes #28248

---

